==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|impenetrabilis|lang=la}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not [[penetrable]].
#: ''The fortress is '''impenetrable''', so it cannot be taken.''
#* {{quote-news|date=2012|author=John Branch|title=Snow Fall : The Avalanche at Tunnel Creek|newspaper=New York Time|url=http://www.nytimes.com/projects/2012/snow-fall/?smid=fb-nytimes&WT.z_sma=SP_SNT_20130415#/?part=tunnel-creek}}
#*: The avalanche spread and stopped, locking everything it carried into an icy cocoon. It was now a jagged, virtually '''impenetrable''' pile of ice, longer than a football field and nearly as wide. 
# {{context|figuratively|lang=en}} [[incomprehensible#English|Incomprehensible]]; [[inscrutable]].
#: ''Business jargon makes this document '''impenetrable''', I can't understand it.''

